       :source-occurrence-id
       "STD3/source/c0d68f7417c5026e583fc882d1ef84f94a93602a1917ee86bafd7bfa24700add",
       :source-path
       "docs/phase-16-standard-library/213-std3-collections-library-specification.md",
       :raw-text
       "The development List provider must reserve bounded first/rest traversal,\ntermination observations and temporary capture before performing them. It must\nnot count or materialize the whole input before that bounded census. Validate\nevery physical Keyword member before member comparison, formatting, hashing or\nSet insertion. A bounded temporary snapshot may then use the existing Keyword\ndeduplication implementation with the remaining budget; all partial capture,\ntemporary construction and returned conversion work remain cumulative.\nThe existing 1024-element and 65536 logical-work guards remain residual\ndevelopment checks, with P15S23X002 on rejection. They are not safety\ncertificates, provider CPU bounds or permission to increase a resource cap.\nTemporary and output storage may allocate, including for empty conversion;\nstored values are shared shallowly with persistent lifetimes and no borrowed\ninput List spine.\n",
       :source-file-sha256
       "58d096cc16d922ad72d560c5b3e4d60d093c9527a9472c2414d63deb98630e3d",
       :id "stdlib/facet/std3/7069-7992",
       :kind :acceptance-rule,
       :document-id "STD3",
       :end-byte 7992,
       :start-byte 7069}
      {:raw-sha256
       "84fd93cc0dcf3b35864fca60e5f8db4caf54e4b8db73e6093575770e78c2c93c",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "STD3/source/6a05e7fc6f6c5597cc8da9655cf536c74aaed76d9501678d13f29c034703d270",
       :source-path
       "docs/phase-16-standard-library/213-std3-collections-library-specification.md",
       :raw-text
       "A Never operand retains the shared Set-constructor non-invocation route. Its\nresult is Never, latent allocation remains possible in the signature, and\ndirect allocation is empty. It establishes no invoked List or Vector domain,\ncount, census, output or cardinality premise. Original source, profile, target,\nbinding and operand effect/capability legality still require validation.\n",
       :source-file-sha256
       "58d096cc16d922ad72d560c5b3e4d60d093c9527a9472c2414d63deb98630e3d",
       :id "stdlib/facet/std3/7993-8374",
       :kind :acceptance-rule,
       :document-id "STD3",
       :end-byte 8374,
       :start-byte 7993}
      {:raw-sha256
       "5d7de1bfb7eb605b4d10d52a4477423ad7a3aa7a93e8581bbfe00820a97ee6e5",
       :source-occurrence-id
       "STD3/source/dbcaed7adf26f51e5b5667089175ee3041ec27acca0d4190f5695f7e1942359b",
       :source-path
       "docs/phase-16-standard-library/213-std3-collections-library-specification.md",
       :raw-text
       "For a persistent Set, `(count items)` returns the non-negative integer number\nof distinct stored members, including zero for an empty Set. It evaluates its\noperand normally, preserves transfers and the original Set, and does not\nevaluate stored payloads. Collection semantics belong to `gravity.collections`;\na `gravity.core` compatibility binding does not change that ownership. These\nrules do not grant arbitrary sequence conversion, every member family or\nprofile support, or Set equality and iteration implementation support.\n",
       :source-file-sha256
